# Normalise text files to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a git configured with core.autocrlf=true — the default on
# Windows, and what a \\wsl.localhost checkout from the Windows side uses —
# rewrites every file with CRLF. Go tooling treats those carriage returns as
# content, so `gofmt -l .` reports the entire tree as unformatted and CI fails
# on a diff nobody made.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the one thing that genuinely needs CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never rewrite binaries.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gz   binary
*.exe  binary
